#### Deforestation outside the community forest

Sometimes when activities are proscribed in one area they may be displaced other areas; an effect known as leakage. To investigate possible leakage effects, we also asked interviewees whether CFM had led to an increase in deforestation outside their community forest (@fig-increased_deforestation_outside).


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![ 'Has CFM increased deforestation outside the community forest?' The length of each bar segment represents the proportion of groups in that category. The numbers superimposed on the bars represent the actual number of groups in each category.](CFMG-SFM_files/figure-html/fig-increased_deforestation_outside-1.png){#fig-increased_deforestation_outside width=672}
:::
:::


::: return-to-summary
[← Return to Summary](Summary.html#sustainable-forest-management)
:::

Contrary to the expectations of leakage, a majority of the FGD groups responded that CFM had actually reduced deforestation outside their CF. This result was consistent across FGD groups and the effect of governance index was not significant (@tbl-M3_deforestation_outside_fgd). Although the effect of FGD type female was significant when compared to the baseline group (Executive FGD), the more conservative pairwise test was not significant (@tbl-pairwise_deforestation_outside_fgd).




