#### Charcoal production outside the community forest

To examine for the possibility of leakage, we also asked interviewees whether CFM has led to an increase in charcoal production outside their CF (@fig-increased_charcoal_outside).


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![ 'Has CFM increased charcoal production outside the community forest?' The length of each bar segment represents the proportion of groups in that category. The numbers superimposed on the bars represent the actual number of groups in each category.](CFMG-SFM_files/figure-html/fig-increased_charcoal_outside-1.png){#fig-increased_charcoal_outside width=672}
:::
:::


As can be seen, the vast majority of groups indicated that charcoal making had either decreased outside their CF or there was no change. However, there were a small number that indicated charcoal making had increased, with some indicating it had increased significantly. Female FGD groups were significantly more likely to indicate that charcoal making had decreased outside the CF than all other groups (CFMG executive members, male or youth community members) (@tbl-M7_charcoal_outside_fgd; @tbl-pairwise_charcoal_outside_fgd). There were no significant differences among these other groups and the effect of the governance index was also not significant.




::: {#tbl-M7_charcoal_outside_fgd .cell tbl-cap='Results of the model examining the effect of FGD type and governance index on perceived increase in charcoal production outside the CF.'}
::: {.cell-output-display}

