### Wildlife

We asked interviewees whether CFM had led to an increase in wildlife inside their CF (@fig-wildlife_increase).


::: {.cell}
::: {.cell-output-display}
!['Has CFM led to an increase in wildlife in the community forest?' The length of each bar segment represents the proportion of groups in that category. The numbers superimposed on the bars represent the actual number of groups in each category.](CFMG-SFM_files/figure-html/fig-wildlife_increase-1.png){#fig-wildlife_increase width=672}
:::
:::


::: return-to-summary
[← Return to Summary](Summary.html#sustainable-forest-management)
:::

As can be seen, a majority of groups indicated a significant or moderate increase in wildlife in their CF. However, there were some that indicated there had been a decrease. The responses among FGD types were not significantly different (@tbl-M11_wildlife_fgd). The effect of governance index was also not significant.




::: {#tbl-M11_wildlife_fgd .cell tbl-cap='Results of the model examining the effect of FGD type and governance index on perceived increase in wildlife inside the CF.'}
::: {.cell-output-display}

